{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MohamedRejeb/Calf/pulls/339","id":2664798809,"node_id":"PR_kwDOKDql7s6e1ZpZ","html_url":"https://github.com/MohamedRejeb/Calf/pull/339","diff_url":"https://github.com/MohamedRejeb/Calf/pull/339.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/MohamedRejeb/Calf/pull/339.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MohamedRejeb/Calf/issues/339","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MohamedRejeb/Calf/pulls/339/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MohamedRejeb/Calf/pulls/339/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MohamedRejeb/Calf/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MohamedRejeb/Calf/issues/339/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MohamedRejeb/Calf/statuses/527cb35344af39d9739378a29da217584bee2248","number":339,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix Bluetooth permissions for iOS","user":{"login":"krzdabrowski","id":36383670,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzgzNjcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36383670?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/krzdabrowski","html_url":"https://github.com/krzdabrowski","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krzdabrowski/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krzdabrowski/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krzdabrowski/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krzdabrowski/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krzdabrowski/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krzdabrowski/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krzdabrowski/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krzdabrowski/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/krzdabrowski/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #205.\r\n\r\nIssues in `BluetoothPermissionHelper.kt`:\r\n- `launchPermissionRequest` was missing the if/else logic (like `getPermissionStatus` does) and was only checking Bluetooth hardware state (`CBManagerStatePoweredOn`) rather than using newer APIs for permission authorization status\r\n- even if `getPermissionStatus` was using the split logic for old/new API, this statement `CBManager.resolveClassMethod(NSSelectorFromString(\"authorization\"))` always returned `false` on my up-to-date iPhone so realistically both methods were using legacy methods for iOS 12 and lower\r\n\r\nFixes:\r\n- add logic for permission authorization status APIs in `launchPermissionRequest`\r\n- decide which API to use (new one is available [since iOS 13](https://support.apple.com/en-us/102267#:~:text=Starting%20in,other%20uses.)) by `systemVersion` property rather than unreliable `resolveClassMethod`\r\n- change invocation for new APIs out of `CBCentralManager`- it doesn't have to be invoked at all (yet, it's still needed to trigger a Permission pop-up)\r\n- add `callbackFired` flag to mitigate multiple callback invocations - basically it should be a one-shot operation if happens.\r\n\r\nI don't do iOS development but I tested these scenarios on my up-to-date real device:\r\n- asking for permissions, then\r\n- granting permissions\r\n- denying permissions\r\n- denying permissions, then changing them in Settings\r\n\r\nAnd everything now works as expected :slightly_smiling_face: ","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2025-07-14T16:39:23Z","updated_at":"2025-11-01T07:23:28Z","closed_at":"2025-11-01T07:23:28Z","merged_at":"2025-11-01T07:23:28Z","merge_commit_sha":"d6c65c3472b97b71abb27f1174a4e6cbae13c003","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"krzdabrowski:bugfix/ios-bluetooth-permissions","ref":"bugfix/ios-bluetooth-permissions","repo":null,"sha":"527cb35344af39d9739378a29da217584bee2248","user":{"login":"krzdabrowski","id":36383670,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MzgzNjcw","avat